Yes they can. You can also use projectiles (thrown daggers, rocks,
etc.).
Only Force Bolt and Striking (spell or wand) will break the boulder.

> Alternatively, should I take the luck penalties by smashing the boulder with my
> pick-axe and then reading a scroll of earth once the unicorn is out of the way
> & the 'd' killed?  (The only spare boulders, unfortunately, were pushed into
> corners when I was looking under them for stuff.  Also, I'm hesitant to break
> illiteracy.)  Any ideas or advice would be very appreciated.

Smashing the boulder and then recreating one is one possible way. But
remember a non-cursed scroll of earth will create a boulder fort...
which can make the situation worse.

Or you can leave and come back with gems and thrown weapons (e.g.
rocks from breaking statues on the Oracle level). Throw gems at the
unicorn - it cannot teleport away, and you can use the chance to ID
gems. Get as much luck as you can - since you already lost some
squeezing around the boulder - and then kill the unicorn (-5 luck) and
the d.

Wand of teleportation will also work, but there's no telling where the
boulder would end up.


